Yu-Gi-Oh! Yu!..

9
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:29,520
Yu-Gi-Oh!

10
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,760
This duel is over, Noah!

11
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:09,180
That's impossible!

12
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,660
I can't lose!

13
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:14,480
I'm afraid you just did,
so my friends are now free!

14
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:21,460
I'm back!

15
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,460
Well, almost.

16
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:26,370
Serenity!

17
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:28,290
Joey!

18
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:29,720
You're all right!

19
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:32,150
Eto!

20
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:33,780
Is it over?

21
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:37,477
Well, it looks to me like everything's
back to normal around here.

22
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:42,720
That must mean Yugi won the
duel. What? What duel? Your duel.

23
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,457
Yugi took over when you and
Mokuba were turned to stone.

24
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,577
Then he combined your deck with his deck.

25
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:49,520
And he beat Noah! My deck!

26
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:53,480
He dueled using my cards?

27
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,397
You've been defeated, Noah.

28
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,637
Not just by me, but by all of us.

29
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:02,177
For it was only with the support of my
friends that I was able to win this duel.

30
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:06,495
And the more you tried to destroy
that friendship, the stronger it grew.

31
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:12,977
This isn't how it was
supposed to happen at all.

32
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,177
Listen to me, Noah.

33
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:17,917
You've been all alone in this
virtual world for six years,

34
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,940
and it's distorted your mind.

35
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:21,570
He's right.

36
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:24,917
I have been stuck in this
digital wasteland for too long.

37
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,317
Maybe the reason I despise
Yugi and his friends so much

38
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,753
is because they share a bond
that I've never experienced.

39
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:36,728
So I tried to eliminate their friendship
to show them what it's like to be me.

40
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:40,080
But they'll never understand.

41
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,517
No one will.

42
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,200
My life was stolen.

43
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:48,397
After my accident, my brain was digitized
into one of my father's supercomputers,

44
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,068
only to be forgotten about.

45
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:53,657
He promised me everything
and left me with nothing.

46
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:55,400
It's not fair!

47
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:58,248
I deserve to be the
president of Kaiba Corp!

48
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:01,720
And I would be if Seto
hadn't robbed me of my life!

49
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,520
I want it back!

50
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:08,897
And I'll start by escaping to
the real world and your body!

51
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,320
From now on, I'm you!

52
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,620
What? What's this?

53
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:15,160
Who are you?

54
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:18,420
Answer me!

55
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:20,800
Your mind is full of secrets!

56
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:26,211
I can see the secrets in his mind as well.

57
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:30,600
That's us, but where are we?

58
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:33,060
What have you done?

59
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,040
Let me win!

60
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:41,320
What are you?

61
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,088
You're not like the others.

62
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,420
Yugi, are you okay?

63
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,460
Try touching me.

64
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,880
Stop it, Joey.

65
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:51,689
Violence isn't going
to get us out of here.

66
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:55,140
You have failed, Noah, so
it's time to set us all free.

67
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,800
And give me my real body back, pronto!

68
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:00,740
So, you want your body back?

69
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:06,917
Your real body's exactly where
it's been since you arrived.

70
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,077
What does that mean?

71
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,657
Enough with the games, Noah.

72
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:11,000
Don't you get it?

73
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,520
There are no real bodies in my world.

74
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,397
Everything here's virtual.

75
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,977
That means all of you, too.

76
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:18,340
I don't get it. I do.

77
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:22,736
We're not just trapped in a virtual
world, we're all a part of it, too.

78
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,070
Exactly.

79
00:04:24,153 --> 00:04:26,637
Your real bodies are
strapped into cyberpods

80
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:29,260
that are hardwired to
my virtual simulator.

81
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:33,700
So everything you've experienced
here has only happened in your minds.

82
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:36,500
So that's why it seems so real here.

83
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:41,014
Our minds are being tricked into
feeling things that aren't really there.

84
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,300
Of course.

85
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:46,620
When the floor opened up, we
didn't fall into a virtual vortex.

86
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:52,820
We were knocked unconscious and
locked in your cyber simulation pods!

87
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:00,500
Now what?

88
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:04,800
You have failed me for
the last time, Noah!

89
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,620
That voice, it can't be!

90
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,060
Father, no!

91
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:10,773
Give me another chance!

92
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,000
Too late for that!

93
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,020
What's going on?

94
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,220
Go Zaburo!

95
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:20,900
Wait, not yet!

96
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:24,200
Father, I need time! More time?

97
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:28,580
You've had more than enough
time to prove yourself!

98
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:31,480
It's time for me to finish things off now!

99
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:37,940
That's why I digitized my own mind when
Seto disgraced me by taking over my company!

100
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,237
I wanted revenge!

101
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,760
Now the time has come!

102
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,157
So, you've been behind
this the whole time?

103
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:47,280
Yes, he has. Right, Father?

104
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,853
And he's going to give Kyber Corp to me.

105
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:52,757
You had your chance, Noah.

106
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,560
And you failed, son.

107
00:05:55,380 --> 00:05:58,080
Look, Pops, you had your chance also.

108
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:03,380
And you failed when you lost Kyber
Corp to someone more fit for the job.

109
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,150
You?

110
00:06:05,233 --> 00:06:07,360
I taught you everything you know, Seto.

111
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,480
You fool.

112
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,617
You thought you could outsmart me?

113
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:14,840
It's about time you learned the
truth about why I adopted you.

114
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,828
After you beat me at chess,

115
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:20,940
I thought you'd be the perfect
person to motivate my real son, Noah,

116
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,600
who was quite a slacker.

117
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,100
So you just used him?

118
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,030
That's not cool.

119
00:06:26,113 --> 00:06:26,943
How mean.

120
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,453
Noah needed to work more on his studies.

121
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:34,585
I thought Seto could give him the push he
needed to someday take over Kyber Corp.

122
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:38,897
But then Noah had his little accident,
and his body was rendered useless.

123
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:42,200
I tried to preserve
his mind in cyberspace,

124
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:45,968
but I soon realized he would
always be the same spoiled brat,

125
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:50,680
unworthy of inheriting my company
So I turned my attention to you,

126
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:54,293
Seto I thought maybe you could
be the heir to my fortune,

127
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,360
so I pushed you to your limits

128
00:06:57,560 --> 00:07:02,580
You gave up on your own son, and you
trapped me all alone in cyberspace

129
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:05,620
Poor guy Not at first

130
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:10,500
Initially, I thought I could still
use Seto to help you. Use me?

131
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:13,679
And what was it you planned
to do with me, Gozoboro?

132
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:18,580
Force me to play chess against your
virtual son to increase his intellect?

133
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:22,120
No, not quite, Seto. Then what?

134
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:26,140
I had something much more
interesting planned. Enough.

135
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,740
Will you spit it out? Very well.

136
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:32,597
Even if Noah could learn how to run
a multi-billion dollar corporation,

137
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,880
he still lacked one major thing, a body.

138
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:38,200
And that's where you came in, Seto.

139
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:39,920
That's sick.

140
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:44,060
You were going to transfer
Noah's mind to Kaiba? Relax.

141
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:46,900
That plan only lasted a short time.

142
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:48,380
Noah's mind.

143
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:53,320
Why would I give you Noah's mind
when yours was perfectly fine?

144
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:58,340
So I concentrated on training you,
Seto, so you could inherit my empire.

145
00:07:58,520 --> 00:07:59,877
But then you stole it.

146
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:02,797
So using the same technology I used to

147
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,586
download Noah's mind
into my computer network,

148
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:07,760
I digitized my own mind,

149
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:11,140
retreating to cyberspace
to plot my revenge.

150
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:16,780
Then I built this place for my final
plan, to take over your body myself.

151
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:21,680
Father, so you used me to trap them here.

152
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:25,617
That's the only thing you did
right, but I'll take it from here.

153
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:28,517
The fun and games are over. You snake.

154
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:32,360
I can't believe that you had
the nerve to call me a snake.

155
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:35,837
I was the most powerful human
being on the entire planet

156
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:40,120
before you came along and stole
that power away from me, Seto.

157
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:44,840
Don't you realize that I treated you
even better than I treated my own son?

158
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:49,620
Thanks for nothing, and I'll make
sure you never regain your power.

159
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:51,160
You're too late.

160
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,700
What's that?

161
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,560
Just look.

162
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,277
It's part of my newest plan.

163
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,977
This is one of the many
satellites KaibaCorp

164
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:01,531
put into orbit when I was still in charge.

165
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:03,758
And what are you gonna do with that?

166
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:08,917
These satellites can beam signals to
every computer system on Earth and

167
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:13,059
connect them back to the underwater
base that holds my supercomputer.

168
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,420
No one on Earth will escape me!

169
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:18,360
I'll have access to
every home on the planet!

170
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:23,440
Please, that has to be the most
ridiculous idea I've ever heard.

171
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:26,020
I'm surprised you feel that way, Noah.

172
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:29,120
After all, the idea came from you.

173
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:32,400
Don't you remember, my son? Hey, Father.

174
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:36,497
I've been working on a new idea that
you might find quite interesting.

175
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:41,345
I figured out how to improve the quality
of the virtual world you created for me.

176
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:43,557
All we have to do is connect our computer

177
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,346
network to other systems
all around the world.

178
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,190
No!

179
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,760
And so, Seto, as you can see,

180
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:53,237
I'm no longer interested in taking control

181
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:56,040
of your body in order
to regain Kyber Corp.

182
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:58,800
I've set my sights on bigger things.

183
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,150
Lunatic.

184
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:03,980
You can believe whatever
you want about me, Seto.

185
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,980
Because once my plan works,

186
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:09,820
I'll be the most powerful
being on the planet once again.

187
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:14,760
And no one on Earth will be able
to stop me this time. Oh, yeah?

188
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:16,500
Seto, no one.

189
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,820
This is about so much more than
just acquiring one company.

190
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:25,037
For when I'm finished, everyone
on Earth will become virtual.

191
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:28,480
I plan to digitize the entire world,

192
00:10:28,740 --> 00:10:32,880
and I will reign as the cyber
ruler of a new planet Earth.

193
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,320
Get back here now!

194
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:44,533
My father's gone for now, but
you have to escape quickly.

195
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:46,737
And I know the way out, so follow me.

196
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:48,597
And why should we believe you, Noah?

197
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:49,797
What choice do we have?

198
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:50,710
There it is!

199
00:10:50,793 --> 00:10:51,840
A possible exit!

200
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,037
Never mind.

201
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:57,717
this is one of several remote
network stations built by

202
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:01,177
my father it can give us
access to all of the program's

203
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:04,397
emergency exits but it seems
that my father has locked the

204
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:07,940
system and closed off every
exit to stop us from escaping

205
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:15,177
when he showed up again after six years
he promised to help me but he was lying my

206
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:18,857
father was using me Kozaburo treated Noah

207
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:21,860
the same way he treated
Seto With no respect.

208
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,230
Wake up!

209
00:11:24,620 --> 00:11:26,340
Noah, are you okay?

210
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:28,370
Noah?

211
00:11:28,453 --> 00:11:30,897
Are you sure there are no
other exits around here?

212
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:33,877
Yeah, maybe there's a way out
of here you're not thinking of.

213
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,897
I've had enough of this monkey business.

214
00:11:35,980 --> 00:11:37,921
I want to wake up in my own body.

215
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:41,857
We got to stop this old man
from digitizing the world.

216
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:43,940
And we can't do that from in here.

217
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,400
Very perceptive.

218
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:49,837
Every virtual reality program has
more than one emergency exit system.

219
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:52,449
So why don't you try
thinking harder, Noah?

220
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,380
What's wrong, Seto?

221
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,017
Don't you want to stay a while?

222
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:59,800
We won't be alone in this virtual
world for very much longer.

223
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:05,257
My father said he's bringing
the whole world in here,

224
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:08,222
and that means I'll never
have to be alone again.

225
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:11,240
We'll be one big happy family.

226
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,440
Noah, stop!

227
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,957
You've got to get a hold of yourself.

228
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:21,569
You're in danger, too, and we
all have to work together now.

229
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:24,320
Moki, you're right.

230
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:26,790
Seto?

231
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,040
Now I think I'm going nuts.

232
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:34,760
Calm down, Mokuba. It's me.

233
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,560
I can see that, Noah.

234
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:42,160
I know Noah's an evil jerk, but it's not
his fault, and I think we can help him.

235
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:43,840
Wait a second.

236
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:46,297
Something has just occurred to me.

237
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:48,860
There is one more escape route here.

238
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,660
Where is it? Tell me.

239
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:55,396
It's a doorway that I created, and
it leads directly to the real world.

240
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:59,220
I'm quite sure my father
has no idea that it exists.

241
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:02,037
You can escape and warn
the world of his plan.

242
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,957
Then what are we waiting around here for?

243
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,760
Let's go. Very well.

244
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,620
Just follow me.

245
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:12,040
Once I claim a body, I'll
be making my escape alone.

246
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:20,780
Come get me.

247
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,080
Well, that was amusing.

248
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:36,360
Now to find those fools.

249
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,740
It's not too far from here.

250
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,520
Kaiba, something's not right.

251
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:48,580
I think Noah's lying to us.

252
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:50,073
He's not to be trusted.

253
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:53,697
Why don't you try telling me
something I don't already know, Yugi?

254
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:57,557
If you're so sure this is a trick,
then why are you following him?

255
00:13:57,640 --> 00:14:00,464
I was always taught to
keep my enemies close by.

256
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,280
Maybe Kaiba's wrong.

257
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:10,500
Maybe Noah is trying to
help us now. But why?

258
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:15,632
His dad betrayed him again, so Noah
must want to stop him as much as we do.

259
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:16,870
Perhaps.

260
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:20,537
Come to think of it, Noah and
Kaiba really have a lot in common.

261
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:25,460
They were both mistreated by Gozoboro,
and they need our help to defeat him. Hmm.

262
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:26,730
You're right.

263
00:14:26,813 --> 00:14:28,820
We're all on the same team now.

264
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,240
So why don't you take it from here? Sure.

265
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:38,055
All right, where is this exit already?

266
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,270
There.

267
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:43,560
Your freedom lies beyond this door

268
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,340
Once you walk through,

269
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:50,187
you'll wake up in the real world
I don't know about this, guys

270
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:56,640
The real world is just beyond these doors

271
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:00,410
Hello?

272
00:15:00,493 --> 00:15:01,480
Where is everyone?

273
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:03,390
Huh?

274
00:15:03,473 --> 00:15:04,303
They're gone?

275
00:15:04,386 --> 00:15:05,960
That's weird Seto?

276
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,280
I hope he didn't leave without me

277
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,130
Mokuba!

278
00:15:10,213 --> 00:15:12,060
What are you still doing here?

279
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:13,554
Where else would I be?

280
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:16,100
They made it out already. Come on!

281
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:17,770
Hmm,

282
00:15:17,853 --> 00:15:19,717
your friends may think they're free,

283
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:22,682
but they're really trapped
in their own memories.

284
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:30,840
This seems oddly familiar, like
I've sat in this exact spot before.

285
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:32,280
Guess who?

286
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:35,300
Hey, you scared me!

287
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:38,000
Hey, I'm trapped!

288
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,520
What's going on?

289
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:41,231
You're finished, Merrick!

290
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:45,080
Not as long as I have Slyper
the Sky Dragon in my deck!

291
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:46,516
Now, Slyper, attack!

292
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:51,080
Buster Blader, retaliate
with your Dragon Sword!

293
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,540
Jam Defender, intercept!

294
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:57,900
Your attacks are useless!

295
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:59,640
It's over for you!

296
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:00,990
Oh, no!

297
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:04,720
I can't let Merrick win my puzzle!

298
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,540
Wait, didn't this duel happen already?

299
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:12,020
What's going on?

300
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,740
We're here, Mokuba.

301
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:20,580
The secret exit to the real world
is located inside this arcade.

302
00:16:20,940 --> 00:16:23,880
Is it inside one of
these video games? Yes.

303
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:26,040
Where is it?

304
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,965
I can't wait to get back home.

305
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:32,440
I'm sorry to say, you won't
be going home, Mokuba.

306
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,777
They're gaining on us.

307
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:35,880
Wait a sec, guys.

308
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,300
Tristan, they'll catch up with us.

309
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:40,520
Look, just take Serenity and run.

310
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:41,622
What about you?

311
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:45,420
I've got some unfinished
business to attend to. Hold on.

312
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:47,380
Come on, move it now.

313
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,600
I'm moving it.

314
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,371
Here, Serenity, this way.

315
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:51,800
It's go time.

316
00:16:57,360 --> 00:16:58,480
Watch it.

317
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:00,237
Cross on the green, not in between.

318
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:03,060
So, what was it you were saying?

319
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:05,240
Um, not sure.

320
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:08,482
Don't you feel like we've
taken this ride before?

321
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,280
Mai, no!

322
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,640
Something weird is going on.

323
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:18,240
Or maybe not.

324
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,561
Everything seems to be all right.

325
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:23,200
Looks like Mai's doing just fine.

326
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,410
Mai!

327
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:28,810
Huh?

328
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,980
Wait, Mai's not just fine.

329
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,420
I remember something.

330
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:37,640
Hello, Joey.

331
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,070
What, you?

332
00:17:39,380 --> 00:17:42,940
Listen, why don't we stop
dueling and just settle down?

333
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:44,960
Stop dueling? For good?

334
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,360
That's crazy talk.

335
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:48,780
Joey, it's just a dumb card game.

336
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:51,620
Alright, I know this isn't real.

337
00:17:56,580 --> 00:18:01,140
Did anyone tell me what's
going on? I don't know. I do?

338
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,149
Noah must have tricked us.

339
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,600
Let's find that punk right now.

340
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,160
Where is he anyway?

341
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,860
Hey, Kaiba's gone too.

342
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,340
And Mokuba.

343
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:14,580
Hey, Noah, I can't find the exit in here.

344
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,960
This video game has so many levels.

345
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:19,657
Do you remember which one you
hid the secret doorway in?

346
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,300
You'll never find out, you fool.

347
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,000
You're close.

348
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:27,377
Close to having your
body taken over, that is.

349
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:28,519
I just remembered.

350
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:31,697
You can't escape with us to
the real world without a body.

351
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:34,660
But I bet Seto can make you a body.

352
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:37,180
I mean, you're our family, Noah.

353
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:42,474
It won't be like your old body, but
at least you'll be in the real world.

354
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:46,097
I'm sure the technology
experts at Kaiba Corp

355
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:48,797
can construct some kind
of a robot body for you.

356
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,780
Hey, maybe we can be twins.

357
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:54,440
After all, Noah, we are
brothers, aren't we?

358
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:59,922
Mokuba still likes me
after all I've done to him?

359
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,120
I almost feel bad.

360
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,322
There are so many games in here.

361
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:06,297
Maybe you hit the exit somewhere else.

362
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,556
I mean, look around.

363
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:10,157
Everything looks exactly
the same in this place.

364
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,070
You're right.

365
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,020
It's over there by that stage.

366
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,050
Up here?

367
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:20,229
This is kind of cool,
but where's the exit?

368
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:21,620
Right here!

369
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,260
I'm free!

370
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:38,480
Finally, I'm free!

371
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:43,680
After all these years, a body of my own.

372
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,020
Thanks, Mokuba.

373
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,160
I owe you my life.
